// Go workspace for the modules that build from public dependencies.
//
// `go work sync` and `go build` here need no NVIDIA credentials, so an outside
// contributor gets the same result as CI.
//
// controller/ and controller/forge-vms are deliberately absent. Both require
// gitlab-master.nvidia.com, and a workspace resolves ONE build list across every
// member, so adding either makes every module unbuildable without credentials --
// including agent, which builds publicly today. They also disagree on the SDK
// version (v0.0.14 against v0.0.9), which a workspace cannot hold at once:
//
//     go: conflicting replacements for gitlab-master.nvidia.com/nvmetal/cloud-api-sdk-go
//
// `make work-full` adds them with the override that conflict needs, for work
// inside NVIDIA. Do not commit the result. See docs/go-workspace.md.
go 1.26.0

use (
	./agent
	./controller/api
	./controller/hack/capd-reboot-controller
	./controller/hack/nico-mock
	./controller/test/e2e
)
